# Compiled *together with* `test.in` rather than instead of it: the
# type check covers `tests/` as well as `src/`, so every import the
# suite makes has to be resolvable for `mypy` to have anything but
# `import-not-found` to say about it. `uv pip compile` unions its
# sources, so this file only has to name the checker.
mypy

# NOTE: `mypy` analyses at the floor `requires-python` declares, so it
# NOTE: reads the `python_version < (3, 11)` half of the plugin's TOML
# NOTE: import whichever interpreter it runs under. `tomli` is `tox`'s
# NOTE: dependency below 3.11 and this plugin's own, but nothing
# NOTE: installs it here at 3.12 -- and an unresolvable import is an
# NOTE: `import-not-found` rather than a checked branch.
tomli
